    "public_publication": false,
    "quote": "A failure rate above 5% triggers a prompt corrective-action plan and retesting; it does not by itself require an automatic market ban. Regulators may set proportionate interim risk controls based on the test results and other relevant safety evidence, and may restrict sales where warranted."
   },
